title: 'fix: refine ExtrinsicBaseWeight calculation'
doc:
- audience:
  - Runtime Dev
  - Node Dev
  description: |-
    # Description

    This PR refines the calculation of `ExtrinsicBaseWeight` in the `overhead` benchmark by switching from an isolation model to a **"Subtraction" model**.

    Previously, `ExtrinsicBaseWeight` often double-counted the overhead charged by `TransactionExtensions` because the benchmark measured a signed extrinsic without accounting for the extension weights that are already defined elsewhere.

    To resolve this, we now continue to use a standard signed `System::remark` (ensuring we benchmark the real production code path including `Executive::apply_extrinsic`), but we subtract the known weights of the signature verification and included extensions from the final result.

crates:
- name: frame-benchmarking-cli
  bump: minor
